{% doc %}
  Section Header

  Shared section heading for the eleven Phase 2 sections and both Phase 3 app
  wrappers. Merchants mark the smile underline by italicising word(s) in the
  richtext field. The marker is semantic, never a visual style — the marked word
  renders upright, because Shopify's Space Grotesk ships no true italics. The arc
  itself is drawn in assets/base.css on .has-smile-underline em::after through a
  masked SVG, so no colour or geometry is emitted here.

  @param {string} heading - Richtext heading. Blank renders nothing at all.
  @param {string} [heading_level] - h1 or h2 (default: h2). An unrecognised value falls back to h2.
  @param {string} [class_name] - Alignment, colour and font-size utilities for the placement

  heading is rendered unescaped on purpose: richtext is markup Shopify has already
  sanitised to its own tag allowlist, and the em marker is load-bearing. Escaping
  it would print literal tags and lose every underline.

  Shopify's <p> wrapper is passed through untouched. It fails the HTML content model
  — a heading takes phrasing content, and <p> is flow content — but the parser does
  not hoist it out, so the paragraphs stay inside the heading and every inherited
  property still applies. Verified in Chrome: font-size, line-height, weight and
  text-align all reach the <p>, and the universal margin reset in base.css leaves the
  blocks stacked exactly one line-height apart with no gap.

  That is what makes a merchant's Enter key work. Each paragraph becomes its own line
  at the design's line-height, using a documented toolbar control. Stripping the
  wrapper instead would weld two paragraphs into one run with no separator and no
  space — "India,one habit" — and would leave a line break authorable only through
  shift+Enter, which shopify.dev does not document for the theme editor.

  Heading colour is set in base.css rather than as a utility here, so that a colour
  class passed through class_name always wins on cascade order. Tailwind's ordering
  within its utilities layer is not controllable from the class attribute.

  For the same reason the default size is dropped rather than overridden: a class_name
  carrying text-hero-heading, text-section-heading, text-strip-heading, text-offer-display
  or text-subheading makes this snippet emit no size of its own, so exactly one font-size
  utility reaches the element and no cascade race decides the winner. The match is a
  substring, so lg: prefixes and -d desktop variants are covered. A size outside that
  list is not detected and would race the default.

  A section needing a non-default arc colour sets --underline-color to a complete
  colour value on its own wrapper, not through this snippet:
  style="--underline-color: #FFFFFF"

  The tabbed-product-collection active tab draws the same arc with no marked word
  through the .smile-underline class. That needs no heading and no call to this
  snippet.

  @example
  {% render 'section-header', heading: section.settings.heading %}

  {% render 'section-header',
    heading: section.settings.heading,
    heading_level: 'h1',
    class_name: 'text-center text-white'
  %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign heading_plain = heading | strip_html | strip

  unless heading_level == 'h1'
    assign heading_level = 'h2'
  endunless

  assign class_name = class_name | default: ''

  assign header_size_class = 'text-section-heading lg:text-section-heading-d'
  if class_name contains 'text-hero-heading' or class_name contains 'text-section-heading' or class_name contains 'text-strip-heading' or class_name contains 'text-offer-display' or class_name contains 'text-subheading'
    assign header_size_class = ''
  endif

  assign header_class = 'has-smile-underline font-primary font-bold'
  if header_size_class != blank
    assign header_class = header_class | append: ' ' | append: header_size_class
  endif
  if class_name != blank
    assign header_class = header_class | append: ' ' | append: class_name
  endif
-%}

{%- if heading_plain != blank -%}
  <{{ heading_level }} class="{{ header_class }}">{{ heading }}</{{ heading_level }}>
{%- endif -%}
